  "id": "voltage",
  "neon": "#5cd6ff",
  "note": "Re-cut to THREE masses after the five-mass version read as noise. The rules it is built to: fewer and bigger parts; ONE continuous glazed band at street level, divided by mullions rather than punched into separate windows; a canopy deep enough that its magenta soffit is what you see from a cab; and exactly two signs — the marquee across the frontage and the roof gantry. The crown takes a different palette so the silhouette carries a light value instead of being one tone top to bottom. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the nightclub arm back.\n\n⚠ RESTORED TO THE HEIGHT OF ITS ARM (2026-09-17). The form above is unchanged and was\nnever the problem; what did not carry across from the nightclub arm was how tall it stands. It was\nat 84% — 1.12x the storey stack against the arm's 1.34x — so every 'h'-tagged field\nhere was multiplied by 1.196 and every 'fh'-tagged one left alone. The silhouette is identical;\nonly the storeys are taller. Same regression as halcyontowers and thespire, same measurement.",
  "pal": "ty_voltage",
